WEBVTT

00:07:59.246 --> 00:08:00.686
among New Yorkers.

00:08:01.413 --> 00:08:04.714
But development around the High Line
was not slowing down.

00:08:05.397 --> 00:08:08.331
A huge real-estate play
called Hudson Yards

00:08:08.355 --> 00:08:11.545
was in the process of becoming
the largest mixed-use development

00:08:11.569 --> 00:08:12.719
in US history.

00:08:13.561 --> 00:08:14.712
In its wisdom,

00:08:14.736 --> 00:08:18.794
the city of New York retained
a small piece of that huge property

00:08:18.818 --> 00:08:21.826
for a yet-to-be-determined
cultural facility,

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:23.466
and asked for ideas.

00:08:24.342 --> 00:08:25.990
And while not the ideal spot,

00:08:26.014 --> 00:08:28.735
we thought, "Why not be opportunistic?

00:08:28.759 --> 00:08:31.625
Why not use the space
produced by commercial development